      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I wonder if there\u0027s a different approach possible to exclude libcore, that doesn\u0027t rely on hardcoding of the libs\n\nAgreed, I would like to avoid a hard-coded list if possible. \n\nBut I am not sure what the right heuristics should be. e.g. conscrypt uses `sdk_version: \"none\"` but currently baselines NewApi errors https://source.corp.google.com/android/external/conscrypt/Android.bp;l\u003d260. If we do not enforce this check there, it may hide relevant errors\n\nAdditionally I think modules that do not use the SDK can also have other dependencies via `static_libs` and `libs` attributes. We probably should still check that the module is not relying on NewApis from those dependencies",
      "parentUuid": "7733a949_055adc35",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "3e2bb84fef43e5da76bcdb0012f8fb95d5dfa4b5",
